  "conclusion": {
    "best_strategy": "DD-Enhanced (defensive)",
    "best_sharpe_diff": 0.0121,
    "any_passes_harvey": false,
    "interpretation": "Drawdown-conditional adjustments do NOT significantly improve 12/VIX. This is consistent with the K458 meta-analysis finding that all \"smart\" adjustments to standard VT yield negligible improvement. The reason: VIX already captures drawdown information (corr(DD, VIX) is strongly negative), so adding drawdown as a separate signal is largely redundant. Defensive strategies (reducing equity in drawdowns) hurt returns in V-shaped recoveries; aggressive strategies (buying the dip) add risk without reliable compensation. The pure mechanical 12/VIX remains the best simple VT approach."
  },
